This python program handles the sandglass transformations problem given in the query. The sandglass contains two bulbs labeled bulb A and bulb B. The initial amount of sand in bulb A is known, and bulb B has the rest of the sand. The sand drops from the top bulb to the bottom bulb at a rate of 1 gram per second. The sandless top bulb is considered as a null container for further calculations. The program stores these information in a dictionary, after which it calculates the minimum number of operations required to see the whole process.

